{"title":"Variables Data Conclat","markdown":{"headingText":"Variables Data Conclat","containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n## Dependent variable\n\nWe measured *political participation* through the variable **c11_02**. *I’m going to read you a list of voluntary organizations. For each one, could you tell me whether you are an active member, an inactive member, or not a member of that organization? Political party*. The variable was coded \"Active\" = 1, and \"Inactive\" or \"Not a member\" = 0.\n\n## Independent variables\n\nThe first independent variable is *workplace autonomy*, which corresponds to the average of items **b06**. *Now, thinking about your current job, please tell me how much influence you have over the following aspects:*\n\n-   **b06_01**. *The methods or ways in which you carry out your tasks during the workday.*\n-   **b06_02**. *The policies your company adopts regarding your working conditions.*\n-   **b06_03**. *The time you start and finish your workday.*\n-   **b06_04**. *The time you are allowed to take a break.*\n-   **b06_05**. *The possibility of taking one or two hours off per week to attend to personal or family matters.*\n\nEach item uses a response scale ranging from \"No influence\" = 1 to \"A lot of influence\" = 5.\n\nThe second independent variable is *union membership*. This was measured through the variable **b21**. *Are you affiliated with a labor union (either company or inter-company) or a public employees’ association?*, coded as \"Union members\" = 1, and \"Not member\" = 0.\n\n## Mediating variables\n\nWe use three mediating variables. The first is *political confidence*, which corresponds to the average of the following items **c10**. *How often do you do each of the following activities?*\n\n-   **c10_01**. *Talks about politics with friends.*\n-   **c10_01**. *Tries to convince someone of your political views.*\n\nEach item uses a response scale ranging from \"Never\" = 1 to \"Very frequently\" = 5.\n\nThe second mediating variable is *political skills*, which corresponds to the average of the following items **c12**. *Imagine that in your community or neighborhood there is a problem with the electricity supply (the power has been out for three days), and the neighbors want to meet to solve the problem. Now I would like you to answer the following:*\n\n-   **c12_01**. *I would feel comfortable organizing and leading the meeting with my neighbors.*\n-   **c12_02**. *I would feel comfortable leading some form of protest so that the authorities listen to our demands.*\n\nEach item uses a response scale ranging from \"Strongly disagree\" = 1 to \"Strongly agree\" = 5.\n\nThe third mediating variable is *identification with political parties*, measured through the item **c09**. *Which of the following political parties best represents your interests, beliefs, and values?*. The variable was coded as \"Left-wing parties\" = 1, which includes Communist Party, Socialist Party, Frente Amplio, Partido Humanista; and 0 = \"Does not identify with a party\" or \"Identifies with right-wing parties\". The parties classified as left-wing are those with a presence in the labor union sphere.\n\n## Controls\n\nOur analyses included the following sociodemographic controls:\n\n-   gender (1 = \"Female\");\n-   age (as a numeric variable);\n-   education level, measured in four groups: 1. Lower (up to completed primary education), 2. Middle (up to completed secondary education), 3. High (incomplete university education), 4. Upper level (completed university education or higher).\n-   sector (1 = private sector; 0 = public sector);\n-   political interest, measured by the item **c10_01**. *How often do you do each of the following activities? Talks about politics with friends* (1 = \"At least once\", 0 = \"Never\");\n-   workplace size, measured in four groups: 1. 1 to 9 employees, 2. 10 to 49 employees, 3. 50 to 199 employees, 4. 200 employees or more.\n","srcMarkdownNoYaml":""},"formats":{"html":{"identi